module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Constructions.SymmetricAlgebraAffineSections
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.FPAlgebraSheaf.Quotient

/-!
# `Sym(ℱ)/ℐ` is a quasi-coherent algebra of finite presentation

Let `X` be a scheme, `ℱ` a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-module **of finite presentation** and `ℐ` a
quasi-coherent ideal of the vector bundle `𝐕(ℱ) = Spec_X(Sym(ℱ))` which is finitely generated
over every affine open. This file constructs

`Sym(ℱ)/ℐ`

as an object of `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.QuasicoherentAlgebra X` and proves it quasi-coherent
and of finite presentation. These are the two conditions [Stacks, Tag 05JS] imposes on the members
of its directed system.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.SymQuotientAlgebra.symQuotientAlgebra`: **`Sym(ℱ)/ℐ` as a quasi-coherent
  `𝒪_X`-algebra** — the direct image of the structure sheaf of the closed subscheme of `𝐕(ℱ)`
  cut out by `ℐ`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.SymQuotientAlgebra.isQuasicoherent_symQuotientAlgebra`: it is quasi-coherent.
* `Stacks.SymQuotientAlgebra.isOfFinitePresentation_symQuotientAlgebra`: **it is of finite
  presentation.**
* `Stacks.SymQuotientAlgebra.isQuasicoherent_and_isOfFinitePresentation_symQuotientAlgebra`: both
  at once, in the shape the directed system of [Stacks, Tag 05JS] consumes.

## Why the ambient must be `𝐕(ℱ)` and not affine `n`-space

`Stacks.FPAlgebraSheaf.polynomialQuotientAlgebra` is the same construction with `𝔸(n; X)` as
ambient, i.e. with `ℱ` free of finite rank. It cannot serve as the member of the system of
[Stacks, Tag 05JS], and the reason is recorded at
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/ColimitGlobal/Basic.lean:51-55`: a morphism of algebra sheaves out
of `Stacks.FPAlgebraSheaf.polynomialAlgebra X n` is, by the relative-spectrum adjunction, `n`
*global* sections of the target, so every polynomial-quotient stage reaches only the subalgebra
generated by restrictions of global sections. On `ℙ¹` with `𝒜 = Sym(𝒪(-1))` the global sections
are the constants, while `𝒜(U₀) = k[t][y]` has a generator in degree one, so no such stage
reaches it. A quasi-coherent `ℱ` of finite presentation which is not free is therefore required,
and it is exactly what
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ModuleLimits.exists_isFinitePresentation_hom_section_algebra`
produces.

## Implementation notes

The construction is
`Stacks.FPAlgebraSheaf.isOfFinitePresentation_pushforwardAlgebra_subschemeι_comp`
applied to the projection `𝐕(ℱ) ⟶ X`, which is an affine morphism
(`AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Modules.isAffineHom_vectorBundleToBase`) and, for `ℱ` of finite
presentation, locally of finite presentation
(`Stacks.SymAlgSections.locallyOfFinitePresentation_vectorBundleToBase`). Nothing further is
needed: over an affine open `U` of `X` the structural ring map factors as the finitely presented
`Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(𝐕(ℱ), p ⁻¹ᵁ U)` followed by the quotient by `ℐ`, which is surjective with finitely
generated kernel.

`LocallyOfFinitePresentation (vectorBundleToBase X ℱ)` is supplied by `haveI` rather than
declared as a global instance: it holds only under `[ℱ.IsFinitePresentation]`, and the general
`vectorBundleToBase` is used elsewhere without that hypothesis.

## Not done here

**The directed system itself is not built.** What remains of [Stacks, Tag 05JS] is the index
poset, the functor into `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.QuasicoherentAlgebra X` whose values are the
objects constructed below, and the two sectionwise conditions that
`Stacks.QcohAlgebraFPColimit.exists_directedSystem_of_affineSections_of_smallIndex` consumes. The
transition morphisms of that functor need a factorisation property of the quotient — a morphism
of algebra sheaves out of `Sym(ℱᵢ)` killing `ℐᵢ` has to factor through `Sym(ℱᵢ)/ℐᵢ` — and no such
property is available in the library at this revision.

**No `@[stacks]` tag.** [Stacks, Tag 05JS] is the colimit presentation; what is below is one of
its two conditions on a single member of the system.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 05JS](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/05JS)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01M2](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01M2)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open CategoryTheory Opposite AlgebraicGeometry
open Stacks.AffineAlgebraEquivalence

universe u

namespace Stacks.SymQuotientAlgebra

variable {X : Scheme.{u}} (E : X.Modules) [E.IsQuasicoherent]

/-- **`Sym(ℱ)/ℐ` as a quasi-coherent `𝒪_X`-algebra**: the direct image, along the projection
`𝐕(ℱ) ⟶ X`, of the structure sheaf of the closed subscheme of `𝐕(ℱ) = Spec_X(Sym(ℱ))` cut out by
the quasi-coherent ideal `ℐ`.

A quotient of a sheaf of rings by a sheaf of ideals is not a sheaf, so the quotient cannot be
formed sectionwise; the closed subscheme is Mathlib's glueing construction and its direct image
is a sheaf by construction. -/
def symQuotientAlgebra (I : (Scheme.Modules.vectorBundle X E).IdealSheafData) :
    X.QuasicoherentAlgebra :=
  pushforwardAlgebra (I.subschemeι ≫ Scheme.Modules.vectorBundleToBase X E)

/-- **`Sym(ℱ)/ℐ` is quasi-coherent.** The closed immersion of the subscheme and the projection
`𝐕(ℱ) ⟶ X` are both affine morphisms, so the direct image of the structure sheaf is a
quasi-coherent algebra. -/
theorem isQuasicoherent_symQuotientAlgebra
    (I : (Scheme.Modules.vectorBundle X E).IdealSheafData) :
    Scheme.QuasicoherentAlgebra.IsQuasicoherent (symQuotientAlgebra E I) :=
  have := Scheme.Modules.isAffineHom_vectorBundleToBase X E
  Stacks.FPAlgebraSheaf.isQuasicoherent_pushforwardAlgebra_subschemeι_comp
    (Scheme.Modules.vectorBundleToBase X E) I

/-- **`Sym(ℱ)/ℐ` is of finite presentation**, for `ℱ` quasi-coherent of finite presentation and
`ℐ` finitely generated over every affine open of `𝐕(ℱ)`. Over an affine open `U` of `X` the
structural ring map factors as the finitely presented `Γ(X, U) ⟶ Γ(𝐕(ℱ), p ⁻¹ᵁ U)` — finite
presentation of the projection is
`Stacks.SymAlgSections.locallyOfFinitePresentation_vectorBundleToBase` — followed by a surjection
with finitely generated kernel. -/
theorem isOfFinitePresentation_symQuotientAlgebra [E.IsFinitePresentation]
    (I : (Scheme.Modules.vectorBundle X E).IdealSheafData)
    (hI : ∀ V : (Scheme.Modules.vectorBundle X E).affineOpens, (I.ideal V).FG) :
    Scheme.QuasicoherentAlgebra.IsOfFinitePresentation (symQuotientAlgebra E I) :=
  have := Scheme.Modules.isAffineHom_vectorBundleToBase X E
  have := Stacks.SymAlgSections.locallyOfFinitePresentation_vectorBundleToBase E
  Stacks.FPAlgebraSheaf.isOfFinitePresentation_pushforwardAlgebra_subschemeι_comp
    (Scheme.Modules.vectorBundleToBase X E) I hI

/-- **`Sym(ℱ)/ℐ` satisfies both conditions imposed on the members of the directed system of
[Stacks, Tag 05JS].** -/
theorem isQuasicoherent_and_isOfFinitePresentation_symQuotientAlgebra [E.IsFinitePresentation]
    (I : (Scheme.Modules.vectorBundle X E).IdealSheafData)
    (hI : ∀ V : (Scheme.Modules.vectorBundle X E).affineOpens, (I.ideal V).FG) :
    Scheme.QuasicoherentAlgebra.IsQuasicoherent (symQuotientAlgebra E I) ∧
      Scheme.QuasicoherentAlgebra.IsOfFinitePresentation (symQuotientAlgebra E I) :=
  ⟨isQuasicoherent_symQuotientAlgebra E I, isOfFinitePresentation_symQuotientAlgebra E I hI⟩

end Stacks.SymQuotientAlgebra

end
